  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response to COVID-19 and Infectious Disease Outbreaks Including Measles and Acute Watery Diarrhoea (AWD) in Target High-Risk Districts of Afghanistan&#x2019;s Provinces (Kandahar, Herat ,Helmand, Balkh and Kunduz)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on existing IOM Afghanistan Migration Health programming and in coordination with the Health Cluster (HC) sub-regional teams in target provinces, this project will specifically support: COVID-19 response and case management, including support to 2 COVID-19 hospitals, the provision of COVID-19 vaccination, COVID-19 risk communication and community engagement including demand generation for vaccines and awareness raising in Kandahar and  Nimroz provinces; Infectious diseases outbreak response with the focus on measles and acute watery diarrhea (AWD) through 8 Rapid Response Teams (RRTs) deployed in four provinces (Kandahar, Helmand, Balkh and Kunduz). Whilst a particular focus will be placed on screening for AWD and measles, RRT staff will also (where possible and feasible) screen (and refer as appropriate) for other infectious diseases, including COVID-19. The project targets a total of 680,480 persons.</narrative>
  </description>
